# tools/al/ales_stereo_tremolo_witness.rish -- stereo_tremolo: the tremolo (triangle LFO on amplitude) carried into stereo, the same swing on both channels -- the rung that OPENS the stereo modulation class (ALES176).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus - the creative suite) - waymark ALES - rung ALES176.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-082400_fill-ales176-lotus-stereo-tremolo.md
# Stands on: lotus/tremolo.rye (ALES74 -- the mono tremolo run once per channel, its TremoloError reused whole and its precheck reused for the up-front atomic validation), lotus/glide.rye (ALES70 -- glide_scale, 256 = unity gain),
# lotus/pan.rye (ALES10 -- the StereoClip), lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 -- the Clip and the one true saturate).
#
# lotus/stereo_tremolo.rye pulses a stereo master's loudness: it runs ALES74's proven mono tremolo on BOTH channels with the SAME swing -- a triangle LFO of depth round centre over period samples driving the scaled GAIN -- the classic
# linked auto-tremolo where both speakers pulse together. A tremolo's swing is scaled units the caller names (256 = unity), not scalars measured across the field, so the same swing on each channel preserves the stereo image for
# free; because each output is its own input times the shared gain g(k), an identical-channel master stays identical and a panned master keeps its pan exactly (the left:right ratio untouched -- the tremolo pulses without wandering the
# image; an offset-phase stereo tremolo is a later rung). Like the stateless EQ shelf/notch/bell and unlike the band-pass, there is no carried state to thread. It validates the swing and span once against the shared length before
# either channel is mutated (BadPeriod on a period not a positive multiple of four or wider than max_clip, BadDepth on a floor below silence, BadGain on a top above unity, BadRange on a span past the samples), so a refusal never
# tremolos one channel and leaves the other torn; TremoloError reused whole. Values only, never a length; the two channels leave balanced. The crux is four laws: the stereo tremolo law (each channel equal to ALES74's mono tremolo
# with the same swing byte for byte, the channels genuinely differing), the image law (an identical-channel master staying identical, a panned pair keeping its ratio), the attenuation law (unity passthrough exact on both, no voice
# louder than the dry), and the balance / silence / atomicity / degenerate law.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_stereo_tremolo_witness.rish

say "ales-stereo-tremolo: Language EN — stereo_tremolo pulses a stereo master's loudness by running ALES74's proven mono tremolo on both channels with the same swing: a triangle LFO of depth round centre over period samples driving the scaled gain, so a steady note gently rises and falls on both speakers together. This is the classic linked auto-tremolo. A tremolo's swing, centre and depth and period, is scaled units the caller names, 256 being unity gain, not scalars measured across the field, so the same swing on each channel preserves the stereo image for free; because each output sample is its own input times the shared gain g of k, an identical-channel master stays identical and a panned master keeps its pan exactly, the left to right ratio untouched, so the tremolo pulses the whole field without wandering the image. Like the stateless equalization shelf, notch, and bell and unlike the band-pass, there is no carried state to thread. It validates the swing and span once against the shared length before either channel is mutated, so a refusal never tremolos one channel and leaves the other torn; it writes values only, never a length, so the two channels leave balanced."
say "ales-stereo-tremolo: Style Radiant — the stereo equalization and filter class stands whole across ALES170 through ALES175: tone, shelf, band-pass, notch, bell, and the swept low-pass, each shaping a signal's spectrum by a coefficient. The other great family of everyday effects points a moving low-frequency oscillator at a target and lets it swing over time — the modulation family: chorus, vibrato, flanger, and the oldest of all, the tremolo. ALES74 built the thinnest such rung for a mono clip: a triangle oscillator drives the gain, so a steady note gently rises and falls in loudness, and because every output sample depends only on its own input sample, it writes in place with no snapshot, no delay line, no lookahead. That thinness makes it the right rung to open the stereo modulation class, exactly as ALES170's tone, the thinnest filter, opened the stereo equalization class. This rung runs ALES74's proven tremolo on each channel with the same swing, so both speakers pulse together and the image is held: because each output is its own input times the shared gain, an identical-channel master stays identical and a panned master keeps its pan exactly, both sides scaled by the same gain so the left to right ratio at every sample is untouched. An offset-phase stereo tremolo, which deliberately wanders the image, is a later rung; this opener is the linked one. The crux is four laws: the stereo tremolo law, each channel equal to ALES74's mono tremolo with the same swing byte for byte with the two channels genuinely differing so no channel is crossed; the image law, an identical-channel master staying identical through the tremolo and a panned pair keeping its left to right ratio at every sample; the attenuation law, unity gain passing both channels byte for byte even at the rail as the tremolo attenuates and never boosts, and no tremolo voice exceeding the dry it scales on either channel; and the balance, silence, atomicity, and degenerate law, an all-silent master tremoloing to silence on both with the lengths held, a bad period, a bad depth, a bad gain, and an out-of-range span each refusing by name with both channels untouched and balanced, and count zero the identity on both."
say "ales-stereo-tremolo: Lens TAME — two bounded in-process i16 clips (left, right), each tremoloed through ALES74's own attenuating triangle gain, the triangle and multiply run in i64 and the write saturating once as a proven no-op since the gain is held to an attenuation; the two channels enter balanced (the StereoClip invariant asserted on entry) and leave balanced (a tremolo writes values only, each length asserted equal and within bound on exit); the swing and span are validated once against the shared length before either channel is mutated (ALES74's precheck, factored out of the mono tremolo and shared, mirroring tone.precheck across the equalization rungs), so a refusal never tremolos one channel and leaves the other torn; StereoTremoloError is ALES74's TremoloError (BadPeriod, BadDepth, BadGain, BadRange) reused whole, the stereo lift adding no fault. The stereo tremolo law is proven by running both stereo_tremolo and ALES74's mono tremolo on the same per-channel content and demanding byte-for-byte equality on both channels while the two channels genuinely differ; the image law proves an identical-channel master stays identical and a right-is-half-left pan keeps its ratio sample for sample after the tremolo; the attenuation law proves unity gain passes both channels byte for byte even at the plus and minus full-scale rail and no output magnitude exceeds its dry on either channel; and the balance, silence, atomicity, and degenerate cases prove an all-silent master staying silent on both, the length held, each of the four refusals leaving both channels untouched and balanced, and an empty span the identity on both; siloed to lotus/, the gain in scaled units rather than hertz, no delay line, no snapshot, no real sample rate, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/stereo_tremolo"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_tremolo.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-stereo-tremolo: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/stereo_tremolo.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-stereo-tremolo: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-stereo-tremolo: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-tremolo' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-tremolo: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-stereo-tremolo line"
